  "known_limitations": [
    "LIST_4A_NOT_PARSED_SUPERSEDED: SUPERSEDED. This gap recorded that List 4A was unparsed and assumed its annex enumerated 10-digit statistical lines needing a separate parser. That assumption was wrong: the annex is 8-digit, and the operative sentence differs from Lists 1-3 only by an \": i)\" enumeration prefix. List 4A is now parsed by the same generalised parser and is in the schedule above.",
    "EXCLUSIONS_NOT_PARSED: CLOSED, not outstanding. USTR granted 840 product exclusions across 11 notices. Only 1.9% (16) name a 10-digit subheading; the remaining 824 are specially prepared product descriptions identifying a SUBSET of a statistical reporting number. U.S. import statistics are published at that reporting number and no finer, so the excluded share of a line's imports is not observable at any parsing effort. Every annex is additionally a raster image with no text layer, and OCR was refused because it would introduce an unvalidatable transcription channel into a legal treatment variable. This is a property of what is published, not a task left undone."
  ],
